  "listingLabel": "Download recovered listing",
  "attribution": {
    "text": "I wrote this in LISP. It runs on LISP 3.72, \u00a9 1981 Ronald L. Nicol, distributed by SuperSoft. Preserved here for small-scale archival use."
  },
  "howTo": [
    "A state is a height (ON or OFF), a hand (GRASP or UNGRASP), and a place (DOOR, MIDDLE, or WINDOW). The player runs one plan when it starts. Try your own at the -> prompt:",
    "(GPS (QUOTE (OFF UNGRASP DOOR)) (QUOTE (ON GRASP WINDOW)))",
    "Two functions are reconstructed: the disk saved PUSH-LEFT and PUSH-RIGHT to one file, and CLIMB-UP and CLIMB-DOWN to another, because file names stopped at the hyphen, so PUSH-RIGHT and CLIMB-UP were lost. The player types mirror images of their partners at startup. The disk and source files are unchanged.",
    "LISP itself starts from the LISP disk, and then the disk holding these functions replaces it, as the two disks were used together."
  ],
  "quickHelp": "At the -> prompt, type (GPS (QUOTE start) (QUOTE goal))."
